===Etymology 3===
Referencing the origin of the name of the {{w|4chan}} imageboard {{w|/r9k/}} (created in 2008), so-called because it implements the {{w|ROBOT9000}} algorithm by {{w|Randall Munroe}} to prevent the reposting of content.

Possibly overlapping with the sense of {{m|en|robot||a person who does not seem to have any emotions}}, alluding to {{w|High-functioning autism|autism}}, due to the prevalence of personal stories describing awkward or embarrassing situations on the board.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Internet slang|4chan}} A habitual poster on the {{w|/r9k/}} board on {{w|4chan}}; a member of the /r9k/ community.
#* {{quote-web|en|author=David Kravets|title=Ominous messages left on 4chan day before Oregon college killings [Updated]|work=w:Ars Technica|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221206041304/https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2015/10/ominous-messages-left-on-4chan-day-before-oregon-college-killings/|date=1 October 2015|passage=One anonymous message addressed to "fellow '''robots'''" hoped readers would have "an enjoyable Elliot Rodger day"—a reference to the shooter who killed six near a Santa Barbara university last year.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Jay Hathaway|title=How 4chan Trolled Two of Its Friends by Framing Them for the Oregon Mass Shooting|work=w:Gawker|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221120003907/https://www.gawker.com/how-4chan-trolled-two-of-its-friends-by-framing-them-fo-1734265649|date=3 October 2015|passage=Posters on the board are locked in an ongoing debate about who can be one of them— a "'''robot'''." Can white guys be '''robots''', despite their privilege? Can black guys? Women love them! It goes on and on. Only one rule really seems to be agreed upon: "If you have no friends and no gf you are a '''robot'''."}}
#* {{RQ:WaPo|author=Justin Wm. Moyer|quotee=anonymous|title=Philadelphia colleges on alert after 4chan post threatens violence Monday|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160624024731/https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/morning-mix/wp/2015/10/05/philadelphia-colleges-on-alert-after-4chan-post-threatens-violence-monday/|date=5 October 2015|passage=It continued: "On October 5, 2015 at 1:00 p.m. CT, a fellow '''robot''' will take up arms against a university near Philadelphia. His cries will be heard, his victims will cower in fear, and the strength of the Union will decay a little more."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Dale Beran|title=[[w:It Came From Something Awful|It Came from Something Awful: How a Toxic Troll Army Accidentally Memed Donald Trump into Office]]|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:All Points Books|year=2019|isbn=978-1-250-18974-5|passage=As /r9k/ '''robots''' posted and reposted Pepes to playfully mock their status as grotesque outsiders whose very visage was disturbing to "normies," they ushered in a renaissance of frogs that soon appealed to all the netizens who every year had a little more in common with withdrawn, internet-soaked hikikomori.}}

